# Data and captures are NOT in git — they are large, binary-ish and regenerable.
# Fallback for these is the dated snapshot in snapshots/, plus the git remote
# for everything that defines behaviour (schema, specs, code).
# NOTE: must be `data/*` not `data/`. Git will not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a negation under `data/` can never re-include anything.
data/*
# Staging files ARE tracked: they are the dated record of exactly what an MCP
# returned, and the Wind fetch cannot be re-run by a script. That provenance is
# the point.
!data/staging/
data/staging/*
# Staging captures are the DATED RECORD of what a source returned that morning,
# which is what lets a price be audited later without trusting anyone's memory.
# Both extensions are needed: Wind arrives as CSV, the westmetall/LME captures
# as JSON. A new capture format must be added here or it is silently untracked —
# westmetall_2026-08-21.json was missed on its first commit for exactly that
# reason, while the adapter's docstring claimed it was version-controlled.
!data/staging/*.csv
!data/staging/*.json
# The Kotak Daily CEMENT Pack arrives through the M365 connector as a
# TAB-separated text extraction of the workbook, so it is a third format.
!data/staging/*.tsv
snapshots/
!snapshots/.gitkeep

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node / front-end
node_modules/
packages/web/dist/
.vite/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets — never commit credentials. See docs/ for what belongs here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated review intermediates — rebuilt by the build_*.py scripts from the
# store, so versioning them would version a copy of data/ which is ignored.
packages/review/_*.json
packages/review/_*head.html
packages/review/*.html
Investment_Micro_System_Audit.xlsx
~$*.xlsx
